{
  "_README": [
    "THE FIELD-ORDER PIN OF 14 section 16.6, PER SchemaVersion.",
    "",
    "*** CHANGING A PINNED LIST IS A SERIALISATION CHANGE, NEVER A TEST FIX. ***",
    "",
    "14 section 16.6, Field order: 'Declaration order of the snapshot record, depth-first.",
    "Adding, removing or reordering a field is a serialisation change: it bumps",
    "SchemaVersion and is handled as a versioned migration, never silently. A CI test",
    "pins the field list per SchemaVersion.'",
    "",
    "This file IS that pin, and SnapshotFieldOrderPinTests is that CI test.",
    "",
    "If the pin fails, a snapshot record's shape moved. Every stateHash ever issued to a",
    "client moved with it, every persisted snapshot now deserialises against a different",
    "layout, and every client mirror stops agreeing with the server. The fix is:",
    "",
    "  1. bump SnapshotSchema.SchemaVersion,",
    "  2. add a NEW entry below for the new version with the new field list,",
    "  3. leave the old entry exactly as it is -- it describes data that already exists,",
    "  4. write the versioned migration.",
    "",
    "The fix is never to edit an existing version's list.",
    "",
    "THE LISTS ARE NOT HAND-WRITTEN. Each entry is CanonicalStateWriter.CanonicalFieldOrder",
    "for that record -- the writer's OWN depth-first traversal -- so the pin cannot drift",
    "from the bytes it guards. The path notation mirrors the traversal:",
    "",
    "    Name              a field of the record",
    "    Outer.Inner       a field reached by descending into a nested record",
    "    Items[]           the element slot of a list",
    "    Map{key}          a dictionary's key slot",
    "    Map{value}        a dictionary's value slot",
    "",
    "and the text after the colon is the slot's DECLARED type, so widening a field, making",
    "one optional or wrapping one in a list all read as the changes they are.",
    "",
    "SchemaVersion 1's list was EMPTY until M1-04, and that was correct rather than",
    "unfinished: PlayerSnapshot and RunSnapshot are M1-04 and M1-05's, and M0-07",
    "deliberately does not author them. M1-04 declared PlayerSnapshot and populated v1's",
    "list below -- the FIRST population of a version's list, which this README authorises",
    "and which is NOT the forbidden 'editing an existing version's list'. M1-05 declared",
    "RunSnapshot and added it under the SAME v1 entry, for the same reason: v1 has never",
    "been read by a shipped client, so the layout it describes is still being written.",
    "",
    "v1 is now populated for BOTH records this milestone authors, so the next addition to",
    "this file is no longer a first population: a snapshot record arriving after a shipped",
    "client exists bumps SchemaVersion and gets its own entry, per the four steps above.",
    "",
    "SchemaVersion 2 is M1-09, and it is the first time the four steps above were actually",
    "walked rather than described. 19 Part G's login calendar needs two fields on",
    "PlayerSnapshot -- the open day and whether it has been claimed -- so:",
    "",
    "  1. SnapshotSchema.SchemaVersion went 1 -> 2,",
    "  2. a NEW v2 entry was added below with the new field lists,",
    "  3. v1 was left EXACTLY as it was -- it describes data that already exists,",
    "  4. no migration was written, and that is the M1 kickoff's ruling rather than a",
    "     shortcut: no migration code exists before soft launch, written migrations become",
    "     mandatory at M18, and until then Player.Rehydrate refuses a row stamped 1 LOUDLY",
    "     instead of reading it against the wrong layout.",
    "",
    "RunSnapshot did not change and is re-listed under v2 unchanged. That is not redundancy:",
    "the pin is per SchemaVersion, and a version's entry describes the WHOLE layout of that",
    "version. A v2 entry naming only the record that moved would say RunSnapshot has no",
    "pinned shape at v2, and the rule that reads it would find no list to compare against.",
    "",
    "Every entry below was GENERATED by CanonicalStateWriter.CanonicalFieldOrder(",
    "typeof(PlayerSnapshot)) and CanonicalStateWriter.CanonicalFieldOrder(typeof(",
    "RunSnapshot)) and pasted verbatim. Do not hand-edit any of them: regenerate, and if the",
    "regenerated list differs from the one here, that difference IS the serialisation",
    "change and the four steps above apply."
  ],
